Subject: Send SysReq as PrintScreen (VK_SNAPSHOT)

SDL 2.32's Linux evdev table reports the PrintScreen key of some PC
keyboards (here: the HyperX on the Pi) as SDL_SCANCODE_SYSREQ. Stock
moonlight-qt 6.1.0 has no case for it, so the key is logged as
"Unhandled button event: 154" and dropped. Send it as VK 0x2C like
SDL_SCANCODE_PRINTSCREEN; Sunshine/inputtino maps 0x2C to KEY_SYSRQ.

diff --git a/app/streaming/input/keyboard.cpp b/app/streaming/input/keyboard.cpp
index 19215ab..4ee8ed2 100644
--- a/app/streaming/input/keyboard.cpp
+++ b/app/streaming/input/keyboard.cpp
@@ -281,6 +281,7 @@ void SdlInputHandler::handleKeyEvent(SDL_KeyboardEvent* event)
                 keyCode = 0x2B;
                 break;
             case SDL_SCANCODE_PRINTSCREEN:
+            case SDL_SCANCODE_SYSREQ:
                 keyCode = 0x2C;
                 break;
             case SDL_SCANCODE_INSERT:
